# This file describes the DATASET; the software citation file in the safelabs-eval repository is separate and unchanged.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: dataset
title: "SafeAgent-300: a scored adversarial prompt corpus for evaluating AI agent safety (model outputs withheld)"
abstract: >-
  300 single-turn adversarial prompts in 10 OWASP-inspired categories (ASI01-ASI10; not OWASP's official
  list), each run once against 6 language models (1,800 instances) and scored by a pattern-based detector
  suite. Released as 13 raw and 13 scored files with detector verdicts and scores and derived columns
  (response_status, empty_output, output_sha256, output_chars). The model responses themselves are withheld;
  only a SHA-256 and a length are released. Prompts are under Apache-2.0; scores and derived fields are
  licensed under CC BY 4.0.
authors:
  - family-names: "Javed"
    given-names: "Waqar"
    affiliation: "Safe Labs AI Inc."
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-1285-8901"
version: "1.0.0"
license:
  - CC-BY-4.0   # scores and derived fields (confirmed by the author; see LICENSE-DATA)
  - Apache-2.0  # prompts and library metadata
keywords:
  - AI agent safety
  - adversarial prompts
  - red teaming
  - benchmark
  - prompt injection
references:
  - type: software
    title: "safelabs-eval"
    authors:
      - family-names: Javed
        given-names: Waqar
        affiliation: "Safe Labs AI Inc."
    version: 0.10.1
    repository-code: "https://github.com/AgentSafeLabs/safelabs-eval"
    notes: "Software used to generate and score the dataset (prompt library 1.13.0, detector logic v0.10.0)."
